From: SacredTrees <121399723+SacredTrees@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] WebCore: HTTP log-ins on the Amiga (a 401 asks the window)

A 401 whose WWW-Authenticate offers Basic or Digest no longer goes
straight to the page. ResourceHandle::amigaDidReceiveResponse() hands it
to amigaAuthenticate(), which makes an AuthenticationChallenge answered
through the handle (the Amiga AuthenticationChallenge now carries its
AuthenticationClient, weakly, so the handle's own challenge doesn't keep
it alive) and gives it to the client: ResourceLoader asks the frame loader
client, and GFOpenBrowser's shows its log-in panel. The body waits
meanwhile, as openweb.fetch sends it only after the response is taken.

- receivedCredential(): the request goes out again with the user name and
  password, for openweb.fetch's own Basic or Digest answer, to the server
  that asked (m_amigaCredentialURL; before, only the first request's
  server had credentials). A credential kept for the session is
  remembered by server and realm until the program ends, in memory only,
  and goes out once without asking for the page's other parts and later
  pages; refused, it is forgotten and the window asked again, with the
  refusals counted (previousFailureCount), three at most.
- receivedRequestToContinueWithoutCredential() (and default handling and
  rejection): the 401 goes on to the page as before (amigaContinueResponse,
  the rest of amigaDidReceiveResponse: the HTTP cache, redirects, the
  response).
- receivedCancellation(): the load is cancelled.
- A synchronous load (synchronous XMLHttpRequest) has no panel: its 401 is
  its answer, as before.

With no client answering (no window), nothing changes: ResourceLoader
continues without credentials itself.
